  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Lentipes ikeae is a small Sicydiinae goby, described in 2014. Adults reach about 3–4 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Native to clear, fast-flowing mountain streams of Java, Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>It inhabits cool, oxygen-rich, rocky streams between 300–500 m altitude. Like others in its genus, it has an amphidromous life cycle (larvae drift to the sea before returning upstream as juveniles).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<ul><li>Soft to moderately soft water; pristine and fast-moving</li><li>pH 6.5 – 7.0</li><li>GH ≤ 4 °d</li><li>KH ≤ 2 °d</li><li>Temperature: 22 – 26 °C (72 – 79 °F); stable, well-oxygenated, moderate tropical range</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Requires strong water flow, excellent aeration, and very clean conditions. Provide smooth stones, pebbles, and high current to replicate a stream environment. Needs a tight-fitting lid — excellent jumper.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous micro-predator — feeds on small invertebrates and biofilm. Offer live or frozen foods such as daphnia, brine shrimp, cyclops, and bloodworms; may accept fine-sized meaty pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful, similarly sized species from flowing waters make suitable tankmates. Good companions include small hill-stream loaches, Stiphodon or other Lentipes gobies, and small danionins or rasboras that tolerate current. Avoid large, aggressive, or still-water fish such as cichlids, bettas, or gouramis.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Males display vivid colors — an iridescent blue-green belly, dark body, and sometimes a bright red band on the caudal peduncle.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/lentipes-sp-ikeae",
      "html": "<p>Because of its amphidromous migration requirement, captive breeding is extremely difficult. It cannot be bred in captivity due to its amphidromous lifecycle.</p>"
    }
  ],
